                                        "entry_id": "12bd8333-d096-37a0-93c9-25702815a072",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A member of an oligopoly; one of a small number of sellers with undue influence over a market."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0b71d39-d7b1-400f-9de4-c4d398cba00b",
                                                "sense_id": "ad1d36a9-72a5-3df9-a36a-b72e510a1648",
                                                "text": "But through the oligopoly, charcoal fuel proliferated throughout London's trades and industries. By the 1200s, brewers and bakers, tilemakers, glassblowers, pottery producers, and a range of other craftsmen all became hour-to-hour consumers of charcoal. This only magnified the indispensable nature of the oligopolists."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3bbcc8d3-f6af-4c04-9928-095d13df120d",
                                                "sense_id": "ad1d36a9-72a5-3df9-a36a-b72e510a1648",
                                                "text": "“As a classic oligopolist, Moody’s earns exceedingly high margins while paying only the needed lip service to product quality.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
